diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index d7a087c..ac9fd9e 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+## 0.5.10 · 2026-11-12
+
+Move in now explains imported people, schedules, coverage comparisons and differences in plain language, and offers Copy details for support. When an adopted schedule prevents undo, the refusal names the schedule. Agents can search and filter incidents and unlinked alerts within their granted services; this is read-only and remains subject to current authority and company policy. Restoring an installation now pauses agents and expires pending or in-flight approvals before the restored records become available. Retained proposals and history stay readable; resuming agents does not revive an expired approval or replay an old action. The pinned rer remains 0.2.108; this update adds no migration. Back up first, keep applied migrations unchanged and keep the existing pager active: paging stays OFF.
+
 ## 0.5.9 · 2026-11-12
 
 Routed keys now show their key ID, ingress URL and a ready sender request. Service integrations let you raise a key allowance and count retained refused-batch notices under Rejected requests. The change-event sample is a numbered recipe with its Node 22 requirement, and Events API samples are easier to read. After restoring an installation, the owner chooser names the administrator instead of showing a raw id. On-call timelines use readable dates and times, and demo weekly covers align with their rota. Incident headers omit empty metadata, and incident and other autosaved drafts confirm when they are saved. Status and rota forms explain invalid entries, refused saves and unavailable actions. Move in can preserve supported saved PagerDuty and Opsgenie email settings as inactive settings, shows differences for review and requires an administrator to choose a service and activate them separately; unsupported rules and active filters must be resolved first. Readiness now includes a dated US installation and dependency checklist, keeping prior evidence separate from what this installation still needs. Incident actions now let responders and administrators prepare, review and export a saved handoff copy as JSON; stale or restored copies need current review, and nothing is sent externally. Agents can read alerts and their retained observations within their granted services, subject to the existing policy and approval checks. Agent approval summaries identify recorded paging changes as live while paging remains OFF. The local hosting guide explains stopping dev and preview and what a deploy dry run checks locally. Not covered: the move-in exporter still needs Node on PATH, and live incumbent exports, delivery and cutover remain unverified. The pinned rer remains 0.2.108; this update adds no migration. Back up first, keep applied migrations unchanged and keep the existing pager active: paging stays OFF.
